WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:09.380
Does a mouse react more to a gentle puff of air because of its brain, or because of

2
00:00:09.380 --> 00:00:11.180
the first neuron in the pathway?

3
00:00:12.060 --> 00:00:17.160
The authors asked this in mouse lines carrying mutations in genes associated with

4
00:00:17.160 --> 00:00:24.800
autism in people. The puff was fixed: 0.9 psi, for 50 milliseconds, on back hairy

5
00:00:24.800 --> 00:00:29.040
skin. The measure was the size of a startle-like movement.

6
00:00:29.920 --> 00:00:33.220
All four mouse lines reacted more strongly than controls.

7
00:00:34.083 --> 00:00:35.723
Then came the restriction.

8
00:00:36.923 --> 00:00:41.403
Advillin-Cre supplies Cre recombinase to peripheral sensory neurons.

9
00:00:41.843 --> 00:00:47.263
That means dorsal root and trigeminal neurons, plus sympathetic ganglion neurons,

10
00:00:47.523 --> 00:00:53.503
not one subtype. Crossed to a floxed allele, it removes that gene from those cells.

11
00:00:54.023 --> 00:00:55.243
The brain keeps its copy.

12
00:00:56.243 --> 00:01:02.103
The team did this for two genes, Mecp2 and Gabrb3.

13
00:01:02.833 --> 00:01:11.433
Deleting Mecp2 or Gabrb3 from peripheral neurons alone, with the brain left intact,

14
00:01:11.433 --> 00:01:14.693
was sufficient for stronger air puff responses.

15
00:01:15.553 --> 00:01:20.493
It was also sufficient for anxiety-like and social-interaction differences, in the

16
00:01:20.493 --> 00:01:24.753
assays tested. Sufficient does not mean it is the whole story.

17
00:01:25.667 --> 00:01:32.587
The reverse test restored Mecp2 mainly in peripheral sensory neurons, on an

18
00:01:32.587 --> 00:01:34.027
otherwise null background.

19
00:01:34.747 --> 00:01:38.307
The driver also reaches sympathetic ganglion neurons.

20
00:01:39.347 --> 00:01:44.347
Tactile sensitivity was rescued, and so were selected anxiety-like and social

21
00:01:44.347 --> 00:01:49.807
measures. Lethality, memory deficits and motor deficits were not rescued.

22
00:01:49.807 --> 00:01:55.027
So the peripheral neuron explains part of the phenotype, and not the rest.

23
00:01:55.867 --> 00:02:03.627
In mouse dorsal horn, GABRB3-containing GABA-A receptors sit on the central

24
00:02:03.627 --> 00:02:09.187
terminals of Aβ and Aδ low-threshold mechanoreceptor afferents.

25
00:02:10.007 --> 00:02:16.887
In sensory-neuron Mecp2 mutants, puncta next to VGlut1 terminals were reduced

26
00:02:16.887 --> 00:02:20.107
by about 70 per cent, counted in fixed tissue.

27
00:02:20.957 --> 00:02:25.927
The authors attributed the touch phenotype to deficient GABA-A presynaptic

28
00:02:25.927 --> 00:02:31.947
inhibition. GABA depolarises such a terminal, and the study reads that as reducing

29
00:02:31.947 --> 00:02:35.847
release. Depolarising is not the same as exciting.

30
00:02:36.800 --> 00:02:39.700
One model does not fit that account.

31
00:02:40.600 --> 00:02:47.040
In cultured large dorsal root ganglion neurons from Shank3 mutants, Ih was reduced

32
00:02:47.040 --> 00:02:48.980
and excitability was higher.

33
00:02:49.840 --> 00:02:53.720
No altered GABRB3 was detected at the terminals.

34
00:02:54.660 --> 00:02:57.200
Same behaviour, different cellular defect.

35
00:02:58.540 --> 00:03:03.940
These are sufficiency tests in one species, and the behaviours are assays, not

36
00:03:03.940 --> 00:03:10.840
experiences. Keep the rule: in these mouse models, part of a tactile phenotype can

37
00:03:10.840 --> 00:03:12.320
begin outside the brain.
